# Recurring Nightmare: "Sacrifice a creature, Return this enchantment to its owner's hand: Return target creature card from your
# graveyard to the battlefield." The target is chosen before the cost is paid, so the creature sacrificed for it is never a legal
# target. Turn 1: Bot1's only creature is a Llanowar Elves and its graveyard has no creature card, so the ability is not offered
# (the first refusal). Turn 3: after Faithless Looting puts an Ornithopter there, the Elves still is not a candidate (the second
# refusal, naming it) while the Ornithopter is (the positive control): the Elves is sacrificed and the Ornithopter returns.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Recurring Nightmare
Llanowar Elves
Faithless Looting
Ornithopter
Plains
Plains x12

